@page "/admin/features"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Optional extras";
    var o = AppOptions;
    string State(bool on, bool ready) => !on ? "Off" : ready ? "On" : "On, but not fully set up";
}
<h1>Optional extras</h1>
<p>Each extra is switched on in the <code>.env</code> file (then restart). They're off unless you choose them.</p>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Write down voice recordings <span class="muted">(@State(o.TranscriptionEnabled, o.WhisperUrl is not null))</span></h2>
    <p>After someone records their voice, a speech-to-text program running on your own server writes down what they said. They see the words, fix anything, and choose whether to add them to the story. Nothing is sent to any outside company.</p>
    <p class="muted">To switch on: <code>FEATURE_TRANSCRIPTION=true</code>, <code>WHISPER_URL=http://whisper:9000</code>, and start the stack with <code>--profile transcription</code>. Needs about 2 GB of memory; on an Intel N100 a 5-minute recording takes a few minutes.</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Answer by replying to the email <span class="muted">(@State(o.EmailRepliesEnabled, o.ReplyAddress is not null && o.ImapHost.Length > 0))</span></h2>
    <p>Storytellers can simply reply to their weekly question email, with photos attached if they like. The reply becomes a draft of that story; they (or you) read it over and press "I'm finished". Replies are only accepted from the person's own email address.</p>
    <p class="muted">To switch on: <code>FEATURE_EMAIL_REPLIES=true</code>, <code>REPLY_ADDRESS</code> (a mailbox that supports plus-addressing, like Gmail), and its <code>IMAP_HOST</code>, <code>IMAP_USERNAME</code>, <code>IMAP_PASSWORD</code>. The mailbox is checked every 5 minutes.</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
    <h2>Paper question packets <span class="muted">(@State(o.PaperPacketsEnabled, o.GotenbergUrl is not null))</span></h2>
    <p>For storytellers who won't use a device: print their next questions, one per page, with lines to write on. When the pages come back, open "Write a story for …" on their page and add a photo or scan of each page to its question.</p>
    <p class="muted">To switch on: <code>FEATURE_PAPER_PACKETS=true</code>. The "Print a paper packet" button then appears on each storyteller's page under People.</p>
</section>
